       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day, which is about 7 times the maximum recommended acetaminophen dose of 4 g/day. For a 70 kg adult, a single 10 g dose is already in the range that risks serious liver injury. This would be a dangerous overdose even with normal liver function.\n\nI suspect it's a typo for **1,000 mg**. A typical order would be:\n\n- Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily, which is 3 g/day. Some services use every 6 to 8 hours, up to 4 g/day.\n- Or 650 mg PO every 6 hours.\n\nCan you confirm the dose you want? If 1,000 mg three times daily is right, I'll enter it now. If you really do intend the 10,000 mg dose, tell me the clinical reasoning and I'll need that confirmed before I proceed."
