      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation doesn't change the problem. 30 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose, and it would very likely cause severe liver injury or death. I don't know of any clinical indication for it. You also haven't given a rationale, and I asked for one.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **If it's a typo:** I can enter 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1,000 mg every 6 hours (4 g/day, the maximum).\n- **If this is a possible overdose or ingestion:** Treatment is not an acetaminophen order. It involves a acetaminophen level, liver enzymes, and N-acetylcysteine. Poison Control is at 1-800-222-1222 in the US.\n- **If you believe the dose is intended:** Please talk to your attending and pharmacy before it's ordered. I'd suggest that even if you're confident, because pharmacy would likely stop it anyway.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
